the matter with me?" I thought. Lo, in my brief sleep, I had turned myself

107
00:08:49,756 --> 00:08:54,399
about and was fronting the ship's stern, with my back to her prow and the

108
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:59,435
compass. In an instant, I faced back just in time to prevent the vessel from

109
00:08:59,436 --> 00:09:04,795
flying up into the wind, and very probably capsizing her. How glad and how

110
00:09:04,796 --> 00:09:09,914
grateful the relief from this unnatural hallucination of the night and the fatal

111
00:09:09,915 --> 00:09:14,159
contingency of being brought by the lee.

112
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:19,999
Look not too long in the face of fire, oh man. Never dream with thy hand on the

113
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:25,518
helm. Turn not thy back to the compass, except the first hint of the hitching

114
